Common failure points include the caller needing to send a Bearer token to the HTTPS endpoint rather than using SigV4 with the SDK's InvokeAgentRuntime (a frequent mismatch when a web app expects JWT auth but the SDK defaults to SigV4), plus CORS issues from browsers. Also worth flagging: Cognito ID tokens carry an aud claim but no client_id, while access tokens have client_id but no aud — so setting allowedClients while sending an ID token would fail validation. I'll present these as hypotheses rather than certainties and keep my answer concise and hedged, since I haven't verified every detail against the docs.

